The period from 1772 to 1828 covers the second half-century of the [[First Republic of Sinchew]], from the election of the first Industrial Party president to the [[Provincial Restructuring Act]] of 1826 and the reorganisation of the provinces.

Its first sixteen years are known as the stalemate years, in which the National Party's predecessor held a majority in both chambers and the Liberal Party held the presidency, and little legislation was made. The period ends with the alternation of the two parties settled into a pattern, the presidency directly elected, and the country's internal boundaries redrawn.

== Parties realign (1772–1777) ==

The [[Industrial Party]] won the presidency in 1772. The [[Lurandian Prosperity Party]], which had been formed out of the split of the Farmer-Laborer Party in 1764, had lost the confidence of the electorate, and the Industrial Party took office.

The two surviving parties renamed themselves in consecutive years. In 1773 the Farmer-Laborer Party became the [[Liberal Party]], distancing itself from both the party that had governed since 1748 and the Lurandian Prosperity Party that had broken from it. The Lurandian Prosperity Party then faded away, its following absorbed by the two larger parties. In 1777, the Industrial Party became the [[National Party of Sinchew|National Party]].

